sequenceDiagram
  accTitle: Admission and retry identity
  accDescr: Django checks identity and supply before a new reservation, releases the database for object upload, and commits queued work only after successful storage. Same-key retries recover the existing logical job.
  participant UI as React
  participant API as Django
  participant DB as PostgreSQL
  participant S3 as Private object store
  UI->>API: 1 POST source + requirements<br/>+ retry key
  API->>DB: 2 Lock owner stream<br/>Recover unchanged key first
  alt New logical job
    API->>DB: Check owner + supply<br/>Rate / active / queue budgets
    alt Admission unavailable
      API-->>UI: 429 / 503 + Retry-After
    else Capacity reserved
      API->>DB: Reserve source/job<br/>+ upload lease
      Note over API,S3: Release DB before external I/O
      API->>S3: PUT exact bytes<br/>Saved-source reuse skips PUT
      S3-->>API: Storage acknowledged
      API->>DB: Lock owner stream<br/>→ document → job
      API->>DB: Commit pending source<br/>+ queued job / outbox / change
      API-->>UI: 202 queued + processing location
    end
  else Same key and input
    API-->>UI: Existing job state
  end
  Note over UI,DB: Uploading = reservation only<br/>Queued = stored + committed intent
